@scene chapter_7c_private_workshop

background: ancient_library.png
music: arcane_study.mp3

dialogue:
"The Enchanter waves a hand, and a narrow door opens in a wall you'd have sworn was solid shelving."
"Beyond it: a small, cluttered workshop, quieter than the great room — as if sound itself is kept out."

background: enchanter

npc Enchanter:
"My private bench. What happens here, stays here. That is not a house rule, {{player_name}}. It is a LAW of spells."

system skill_learned:
"MODULE UNLOCKED"
"THE PRIVATE WORKSHOP"
"local vs global · reading out · why assigning surprises you"

dialogue:
"— LESSON I — READING THE HALL —"

npc Enchanter:
"A spell cast in here can still SEE what sits out in the main hall. Reading outward is allowed."

interactive: workshop_read_global

dialogue:
"— LESSON II — THE SURPRISE —"

npc Enchanter:
"But the moment you set a name in here, you make a PRIVATE copy — on this bench, for this casting only."
"Change it all you like. The thing of the same name out in the hall never feels a thing. This ruins more apprentices than any monster."

interactive: workshop_shadow

dialogue:
"— LESSON III — SECRETS STAY —"

npc Enchanter:
"And what is BORN in here dies in here. Ask for it out in the hall and the world shrugs — it never heard the name."

interactive: workshop_local_gone

npc Enchanter:
"So learn to tell, at a glance, which names live INSIDE a spell and which live out in the open."

interactive: workshop_sort

dialogue:
"— PROVE IT — WORK ON YOUR OWN BENCH —"

npc Enchanter:
"Bind me a spell that does everything on its OWN bench and hands back the result. It reaches for nothing outside. Clean. Contained."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Write brew(strength): make a local potion (strength * 3) and return it."

mission: workshop_scope

dialogue:
"Your spell works entirely within itself, and passes back exactly one clean result."
"The Enchanter nods, then — for the first time — his eyes flick toward the floor, and the amusement leaves his face."

npc Enchanter:
"Good. You bind, you keep your secrets, you leave no mess."
"There was one last spell I meant to teach you slowly, over a warm winter."

interactive: workshop_final_recall

npc Enchanter:
"But it is not going to be a warm winter."
"Come back to the main room, {{player_name}}. Quickly. Something has followed you up the mountain."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Private Workshop"
"Mastered: local vs global · reading a global · why assigning makes a local"

reward:
xp: 60
gold: 30
achievement: WHAT HAPPENS IN THE WORKSHOP

next:
chapter_7_enchanters_bargain
